description:
Add new App Group keys to `AppGroupConstants.swift` for Dashboard data sharing between main app and `DeenFirstActivityReport` extension.

```swift
// Date-keyed (yyyy-MM-dd)
static func quranSecondsKey(_ date: String) -> String { "deen.\(date).quranSeconds" }
static func focusSessionsKey(_ date: String) -> String { "deen.\(date).focusSessions" }
static func recitationsPassedKey(_ date: String) -> String { "deen.\(date).recitations.passed" }
static func recitationsAttemptsKey(_ date: String) -> String { "deen.\(date).recitations.attempts" }

// ISO week-keyed (yyyy-Www)
static func emergencyUnblocksKey(_ week: String) -> String { "deen.\(week).emergencyUnblocks" }

// Global
static let streakCurrentKey = "deen.streak.current"
static let streakLongestKey = "deen.streak.longest"
static let dataLastUpdatedAtKey = "deen.data.lastUpdatedAt"
static let lastKnownDateKey = "lastKnownDate"
```

**Acceptance criteria:**

* All keys added with no typos
* Date/week helper functions return correct format strings
* No conflicts with existing keys

**Blocks:** M5-1 (DashboardDataWriter), M5-3 (DeenScoreCalculator)

Create `DashboardDataWriter.swift` in `Domain/Services/`. Writes Quran engagement data to the shared App Group container after every qualifying event.

**Methods:**

```swift
func recordFocusSession(duration: TimeInterval)
func recordQuranReading(duration: TimeInterval)
func recordRecitationPassed()
func recordRecitationAttempt()
func recordEmergencyUnblock()
func updateStreak(_ current: Int, longest: Int)
func flush()  // safety sync — call on every app foreground
```

**Key format:** Date-keyed using `AppGroupConstants.quranSecondsKey(date:)` etc. Date string = ISO `yyyy-MM-dd`. Week string = ISO `yyyy-Www`.

**All writes are additive** (+=), not overwrites, except streak (set directly).

**Also write:** `dataLastUpdatedAt` = ISO8601 timestamp on every write (staleness check for extension).

**Register in DIContainer.**

**Acceptance criteria:**

* All methods write to correct App Group keys
* Additive writes accumulate correctly across calls
* flush() syncs current streak + dataLastUpdatedAt
* Extension can read written values (verify via shared defaults)
